# nginx Basic-auth credentials for this gate — TEMPLATE ONLY (this .example is
# tracked; the real `.htpasswd` next to it is gitignored and must NOT be committed).
#
# The real file holds a bcrypt hash and is COPYed into the image by ui.Dockerfile.
# Generate a UNIQUE credential PER GATE (do not reuse one hash across live/lab/forge),
# at a modern cost, then write it to `.htpasswd` in this directory:
#
#   htpasswd -B -C 12 -c deploy/hunter-lab/nginx/.htpasswd <username>
#
#   -B         bcrypt (not the weak default)
#   -C 12      cost 12 (raise the previous cost-05 hash)
#   -c         create the file (omit -c to add more users to an existing file)
#
# Rotate whenever it may have leaked. Never share the same hash between gates.
